{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Behold, I have given you every herb bearing seed</b> — He did not permit Adam and his wife to kill a creature and to eat flesh; rather, every green herb they shall eat, all of them together. But when the sons of Noah came, He permitted them flesh, as it is said (Genesis 9:3): \"Every moving thing that lives shall be for food for you; as the green herb have I given you all\" — as the green herb that I permitted to the first Adam, I have permitted you all. This is the language of Rashi. And thus the Rav explained in the tractate of Sanhedrin (59a, s.v. לא הותר): \"And to every beast of the earth\" — to you and to the beasts I have given the grasses and the trees, and \"every green herb for food.\" But if so, the meaning of \"every green herb for food\" would be \"and every green herb.\" And this is not so. Rather, He gave to Adam and his wife \"every herb bearing seed\" and every fruit of a tree, and to the beast of the earth and to the bird of the sky He gave \"every green herb\" — not the fruit of the tree and not the seeds, and their food is not all alike. But flesh they were not permitted until the sons of Noah, according to the opinion of our Sages, and this is the plain sense of Scripture.\n\nAnd this was because possessors of a soul of movement have some superiority in their soul — they are likened in it to possessors of the rational soul, and they have choice in their welfare and their sustenance, and they flee from pain and death, and Scripture says: \"Who knows the spirit of the sons of man, whether it goes upward, and the spirit of the beast, whether it goes downward beneath the earth\" (Ecclesiastes 3:21). And when they sinned and all flesh corrupted its way upon the earth, and it was decreed that they would die in the Flood, but for the sake of Noah He saved from them for the perpetuation of the species; He granted them permission to slaughter and to eat, for their perpetuation was on his account. Yet despite all this He did not grant them permission over the soul itself, and He forbade them a limb from a living animal. And He further added for us in the commandments to forbid all blood, because it is the stand of the soul, as it is written (Leviticus 17:14): \"For the soul of all flesh is in its blood; and I said to the children of Israel: the blood of all flesh you shall not eat, for the soul of all flesh is its blood\" — for He permitted the body of a living creature that does not speak after death, but not the soul itself. And this is the reason for slaughter, and what they said (Bava Metzia 32b): \"suffering of animals is a Torah law,\" and this is our blessing that we recite: \"who has sanctified us with His commandments and commanded us concerning slaughter.\" And I will speak further regarding the matter of the commandment concerning blood when I arrive there (Leviticus 17:11–14), if HaShem will grant me to complete it.\n\nAnd the reason for \"every herb bearing seed, and every tree in which is the fruit of a tree bearing seed — to you it shall be for food\" is that they shall eat the seed of the herb, such as grains of wheat and barley and legumes and others, and they shall eat every fruit of the tree, but the tree itself is not for them for food, and neither is the herb — until Adam was cursed and it was said to him: \"and you shall eat the herb of the field\" (Genesis 3:18)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The Rav's citation refers to Maimonides' position in Guide for the Perplexed; the Sanhedrin 59a reference is to the Talmudic discussion. Ramban quotes Rashi's language and Maimonides' interpretation, then offers his own reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-21T22:15:35.578583567Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}